The Nautilus developers are engaged in active development on one of the project repositories located at /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/demo. 
During testing, several test branches were created, and now they require cleanup. Here are the requirements provided to the DevOps team:
On the Storage server in Stratos DC, delete a branch named xfusioncorp_demo from the /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/demo Git repository.

SOLUTION
cd /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/demo
sudo git branch
Exactly — the issue now is that xfusioncorp_demo is the currently checked-out branch in that worktree. Git will not delete the branch you're currently on.

Switch to master first:

sudo git checkout master

Then delete the branch:

sudo git branch -D xfusioncorp_demo

Finally verify:

sudo git branch

You should see:

* master

and xfusioncorp_demo should be gone.

Why this happened

You currently have:

  master
* xfusioncorp_demo

The * means you are currently on xfusioncorp_demo. Git requires you to switch to another branch before deleting it.

So the exact sequence is:

cd /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/demo
sudo git checkout master
sudo git branch -D xfusioncorp_demo
sudo git branch

No global safe.directory configuration is needed.
